    "notes": "SAB closed score: Soprano (stems up) and Alto (stems down) share the treble staff; the Baritone is alone on the bass staff (its stems point both ways and must NOT be split into two parts). In m.4 the alto line moves down onto the bass staff (c#' then a, stems up, above the baritone's down-stem notes) while the soprano is alone on the treble staff: those two alto notes belong to the Alto part, not to the Baritone and not to a new part. Expected output: exactly 3 parts. Two verses under the treble staff, aligned to the Soprano (truth: Soprano only)."
  },
